Fix critical payment flow: donations marked failed despite successful payment

Root cause analysis:
- Al Rajhi callbacks reach the server but decryption was failing (DECRYPT_ERROR)
  or the callback URL was unreachable → donations stayed "pending" → 3-hour
  expiry cron marked them as "failed" with paymentStatus still "pending"
- The inquiry endpoint was short-circuiting on "failed" status without querying
  the gateway, preventing recovery of wrongly-failed payments

Fixes applied:
1. rajhiInquiry (server): No longer short-circuits on "failed" donations.
   Within 24 hours, always re-queries the Al Rajhi gateway (action 8) even for
   failed donations. This allows recovering payments the cron wrongly expired.
2. rajhiRecoverPending (server): Now includes "failed" donations (within 48h)
   in addition to "pending" ones in the batch recovery query.
3. handleRajhiCallback (server): Added Fallback 2 — when callback decryption
   fails AND plain "Response" field is not success, now directly queries the
   gateway (inquiry) as a last resort before leaving as "pending".
4. PaymentResult.tsx (frontend): Starts in "polling" mode even when URL says
   "failed" (not just "pending"). Immediately triggers inquiry after first DB
   fetch if status is failed/pending. This recovers wrongly-failed payments
   without requiring the user to do anything.
5. isSuccessResult (rajhi.ts): Added more success codes ("1", "SUCCESS",
   "SUCCESSFUL", "OK") and prefix matches ("CAPTURED...", "APPROVED...").
6. Fixed donations data extraction in Profile.tsx and employee/Dashboard.tsx
   to handle {success, donations, total} API response shape.
